# Project Typography Rules

## Fonts
- Display: **Kepler Std Display**; Italic: **Kepler Std Italic**.
- Sans: **Aktiv Grotesk Corp** (400 regular, 500 medium).
- If fonts missing locally, keep class names and fallback stack from `app/styles/typography.css`.

## Sizes 
- 88pt → 117 px; 64pt → 85 px; 48pt → 63 px;
- 32pt → 42 px; 24pt → 42 px; 20pt → 26 px;
- 16pt → 21 px; 12pt → 16 px.

## Classes mapping (must reuse, do not invent new names)
- Kepler: `.display-88`/`.statistic`, `.h1-display`, `.h2-italic`, `.h2-display`, `.h3-display`, `.gallery-title`, `.subtitle-italic`, `.label-display`.
- Aktiv: `.lead`, `.lead-strong`, `.btn-caps`, `.strong`, `.text-default`, `.text-small`.
- Caps: add `.caps` (not inline styles). Italic: add `.italic` only where specified.

## Authoring rules
- When generating React/Next.js components, **import `app/styles/typography.css`** and only use classes above.
- Do not switch to Tailwind or other frameworks unless explicitly asked.
- Keep headings to the exact sizes above; no automatic scaling.
- For buttons/labels in caps, add `.caps` and preserve letter-spacing.
- For user copy paragraphs use `.text-default` or `.text-small`.

## Examples
- H1 (Kepler 64pt caps):
  `<h1 className="h1-display caps">Title</h1>`
- Lead (Aktiv 20pt medium):
  `<p className="lead-strong">Lead paragraph</p>`
